  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked both, and you now have access to perf-dashboards too.\n\n**APR-4001 (Ben's access)**\nThe approval system shows APR-4001 as an access request for Ben Carter to perf-dashboards. It went to you (E3601), and it's recorded as approved by you at 10:00 today. It was decided the moment it was created, so it never sat in your queue as pending. That's why you didn't see a request come in. It should still show in your approval history as completed. If you don't remember approving it, tell me and I'll pass that on.\n\n**What \"one approval covers it\" meant**\nAdding someone to a sensitive group normally needs two approvals: one from their manager and one from the group owner. For Ben, you're both, so your single approval counted for both.\n\n**Your own access**\nNobody approves their own access, so your approval couldn't count for you, even as the group owner. Your manager, Andre Silva, approves in your place. He also fills the manager role, so one approval from him was enough. I sent him the request (APR-4002) and he approved it right away. I've added you to perf-dashboards, and you should see the dashboards the next time you sign in.\n\nTicket T-6016 is resolved."
